  "term": "transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation",
  "definition": "Transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation is a noninvasive procedure that delivers electrical current from an outside device through skin pads to stimulate peripheral nerves. It is most often used for peripheral nerve pain, but it may be used for other purposes as well.",
